@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-config Configuration
@brief Configuration macros.

@details
The µTest++ Testing Framework library uses several preprocessor macros
to enable it and to configure various options.

These macros must be defined by the application; neither the library nor
its CMake, meson, and xPack build files define them (the `defaultDefine`
entries in `xcdl-package.jsonc` are informative only).

The preferred place is `micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus-defines.h`, or
`micro-os-plus/project-config.h`, which each µTest++ header includes, if
present, before its own definitions, so that the application and the
library sources are compiled with the same configuration. The macros
have no value, only their definition matters; guard them, so that they
can also be defined on the compiler command line:

@code{.cpp}
#if !defined(MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_ENABLED)
#define MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_ENABLED
#endif // !defined(MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_ENABLED)
@endcode

A macro defined only on the compiler command line (for example
`‑DMICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_ENABLED`) must be defined for the 
entire build (both the application and the library sources).
